[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags:** none. There is no init function, no context
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m struct, no setter, no global, no environment lookup and no `#ifdef` in either
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `sieve.c` or `sieve.h` (verified by the grep recorded in `ERRORS.md`). The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m library is stateless and its only configuration axis is the single `int`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m argument.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Branches the C actually takes** (the whole control flow):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. `while (1)` — unconditional loop.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. `printf("%d\n", val)` — output width/format varies with the value's digit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     count and sign; this is a data-shape axis, exercised below.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. `if (val % 10 == 9) break;` — the only conditional. With C's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     truncating `%`, the predicate is reachable-true **only** for non-negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     `val` whose last decimal digit is 9. For negative `val` the remainder is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     `<= 0`, so the predicate is always false and the loop runs up through zero
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     to `9`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. `val++` — signed increment; wraps at `INT_MAX` in the compiled code.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the meaningful axes are: **sign** (negative / zero / positive) x
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **residue `val % 10`** (which decides 1-iteration vs multi-iteration) x
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **magnitude / digit-width shape** (single digit, digit-width transitions,
